    'LET PETER ANSWER: THE ROCK, THE KEYS, AND THE GATES THAT CANNOT HOLD. Men have argued for centuries about one sentence Jesus spoke on a road in the north: "And I say also unto thee, That thou art Peter, and upon this rock I will build my church; and the gates of hell shall not prevail against it." (Matthew 16:18) The argument asks who the rock is. There is a better way to ask it, and it is the Word’s own way: let the man in the sentence answer. Peter preached, and Peter wrote, and in both he says plainly what the foundation is — and it is not himself. We do not settle this by taking a side. We settle it by opening the Book to the places Peter himself speaks.',
